    "['isis ipv6 enable [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface <interface_name> ipv6 enable', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols isis interface <interface_name> ipv6 enable\\n##\\n\\nNote: In the Juniper translation, you would replace `<interface_name>` with the actual interface name (e.g., `ge-1/0/0` or `ge-1/0/4`). The command enables IS-IS IPv6 routing on the specified interface for the IS-IS instance (though Juniper doesn't use instance numbers in the same way as Huawei). \\n\\nIf you need to specify the IS-IS level (level-2 in the Huawei config), you would additionally use:\\n`set protocols isis level 2 enable` at the global configuration level.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface <interface_name> ipv6 enable'}]]": 1,
