    "['isis ipv6 enable [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name> ipv6-router-id <ipv6_address>', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `isis ipv6 enable 2`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name> ipv6-router-id <ipv6_address>\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name> level 2\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Juniper, you need to specify the interface name in place of `<interface-name>`\\n2. You also need to specify an IPv6 address as router-id in place of `<ipv6_address>`\\n3. The `level 2` corresponds to the IS-IS instance level 2 in the HUAWEI configuration\\n\\nThe exact interface and IPv6 address would depend on your specific network setup. For a more precise translation, you'd need to substitute these placeholders with actual values from your configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name> ipv6-router-id <ipv6_address>'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name> level 2', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `isis ipv6 enable 2`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name> ipv6-router-id <ipv6_address>\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name> level 2\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Juniper, you need to specify the interface name in place of `<interface-name>`\\n2. You also need to specify an IPv6 address as router-id in place of `<ipv6_address>`\\n3. The `level 2` corresponds to the IS-IS instance level 2 in the HUAWEI configuration\\n\\nThe exact interface and IPv6 address would depend on your specific network setup. For a more precise translation, you'd need to substitute these placeholders with actual values from your configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name> level 2'}]]": 1,
